# What gets deployed: web/ (static) and api/screener.py (one Python function),
# plus the pure modules that function imports -- collectors/, filters/, scoring/
# and prompts/score.md, which it reads for prompt_version.
#
# pyproject.toml stays excluded on purpose. It declares duckdb and requests, and
# the deployed function needs neither: it is stdlib-only so there is nothing to
# install at build time. Letting the builder see a dependency list would add an
# install step whose only possible contribution is a new way for the deploy to
# fail.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
requirements.txt

# Not deployed: the collector's own tooling and its data.
calibration/
tests/
fixtures/
data/
.venv/
.claude/
.github/
export_web.py
deploy.ps1
BUILD_BRIEF.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
